{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_ebfe29bcebd828f3a40cffeac82c3aef913bc4ad8ffbfdb9a2551fe967b598f1"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"requirements.txt lists litellm, python-dotenv, PyYAML, tiktoken, openai, anthropic, google-generativeai, gradio, docker, Jinja2, pydantic, watchdog, termcolor, requests, and typing-extensions as core libraries, plus pytest."}],"claim_ids":["clm_ebfe29bcebd828f3a40cffeac82c3aef913bc4ad8ffbfdb9a2551fe967b598f1"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:40:11Z","created_by_operation":"op_300325db995647a2b983cdb81a020b6b","id":"pg_b07ee15f61d356b48b3700e71fbb4a09","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/shyamsaktawat-openalpha-evolve-requirements-txt-0389aea0e0a7-00e71fbb4a09.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_1a0d70fe6b4d5f2084fc2f33ca2cabae"],"title":"shyamsaktawat/OpenAlpha_Evolve/requirements.txt @ 0389aea0e0a7","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:40:11Z","updated_by_operation":"op_300325db995647a2b983cdb81a020b6b"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[],"claim_ids":[],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:40:11Z","created_by_operation":"op_300325db995647a2b983cdb81a020b6b","id":"pg_b86fd38377295f44834b5ca80160cd2b","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/shyamsaktawat-openalpha-evolve-license-md-0389aea0e0a7-5ca80160cd2b.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_c47b4ffac2e4566eb69f5d522181251d"],"title":"shyamsaktawat/OpenAlpha_Evolve/LICENSE.md @ 0389aea0e0a7","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:40:11Z","updated_by_operation":"op_300325db995647a2b983cdb81a020b6b"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_0470886912073b1ea830fb09cd8cfedfda1ccf6f349ad9204baa7357ea6a5c2c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The DatabaseAgent stores programs with code, fitness scores, generation, and lineage as a record of evolutionary history; the README notes this storage is currently in-memory."},{"claim_ids":["clm_2d17cbaacef4034af336c7036a360980cdfa1ba58a500159940345894d9b8286"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The README's disclaimer states this is an experimental project whose generated code may not always be optimal, correct, or secure, and should be reviewed and tested thoroughly before production use."},{"claim_ids":["clm_48c202c3ce22f3b37976a2cd5e94b20d6485fcba6b40620d8ae663c32e614a9a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Per the README feature list, generated code is executed in Docker containers for sandboxed evaluation, with configurable timeout mechanisms."},{"claim_ids":["clm_4dcb233eec2d76efe1d0c6d69be71ef878aa36f552b92a7b53e3b7a4b4076e5c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The system uses a modular agent architecture with named agents: PromptDesignerAgent, CodeGeneratorAgent, EvaluatorAgent, DatabaseAgent, SelectionControllerAgent, and a task_manager agent that orchestrates the evolutionary loop and coordinates the others."},{"claim_ids":["clm_656ee61ec88e72d115cd2a81cab3dedc00b97cbb46480cc385bd7143abc55fff"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The CLI entry point runs an evolutionary run via 'python -m main <task.yaml>' (e.g., examples/shortest_path.yaml), with logs also saved to alpha_evolve.log by default."},{"claim_ids":["clm_6bf311b4dca724d03b43287b96a02a33c550507a14b64c2b6ee2cdb0e439e31c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Mutation and bug-fix prompts often request changes in diff format, and the code generator attempts to apply received diffs to the parent code; the features list describes diff-based mutations for targeted modifications."},{"claim_ids":["clm_710932ecc951899eeb3f531edcef1c32a113e5a202758f0c3d54086eb987e9bf"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: contributors are asked to report bugs or suggest features via GitHub issues, and to fork the repo, create a feature branch, write clean documented code, add tests if applicable, avoid breaking existing functionality, and submit pull requests with clear descriptions."},{"claim_ids":["clm_b79a1dc768c450e1c2cad875a871deee50bb57fb581b1e65bff04c336a67a628"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The EvaluatorAgent syntax-checks generated code, executes it in an isolated environment against task input/output examples, and scores fitness based on correctness (test cases passed), runtime efficiency, and other potential metrics."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ecaa41cd141de451dc72c16f4ca94312bbdb29e0e16e2a60f65b482eddce663b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A Gradio web interface is started with 'python app.py'; it displays a local URL (e.g., http://127.0.0.1:7860) and optionally a public share link, where users can define custom tasks and run evolution interactively."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f39c37f4e2d1eb652be0cdf29566f1a8b473f6d390ad233480d9fccf288da4b2"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The README prerequisites require Python 3.10+, pip, git, and a running Docker installation (Docker Desktop on Windows/Mac or Docker Engine on Linux) for sandboxed code evaluation."}],"claim_ids":["clm_0470886912073b1ea830fb09cd8cfedfda1ccf6f349ad9204baa7357ea6a5c2c","clm_2d17cbaacef4034af336c7036a360980cdfa1ba58a500159940345894d9b8286","clm_48c202c3ce22f3b37976a2cd5e94b20d6485fcba6b40620d8ae663c32e614a9a","clm_4dcb233eec2d76efe1d0c6d69be71ef878aa36f552b92a7b53e3b7a4b4076e5c","clm_656ee61ec88e72d115cd2a81cab3dedc00b97cbb46480cc385bd7143abc55fff","clm_6bf311b4dca724d03b43287b96a02a33c550507a14b64c2b6ee2cdb0e439e31c","clm_710932ecc951899eeb3f531edcef1c32a113e5a202758f0c3d54086eb987e9bf","clm_b79a1dc768c450e1c2cad875a871deee50bb57fb581b1e65bff04c336a67a628","clm_ecaa41cd141de451dc72c16f4ca94312bbdb29e0e16e2a60f65b482eddce663b","clm_f39c37f4